    <summary>Free CLI tool for downloading YouTube videos and audio</summary>
    <description>
# pull-vids

A free, open-source CLI tool for downloading YouTube videos and audio. Inspired by tools like Downie and PullTube, but completely free!

## Features

- Download YouTube videos in various qualities (360p to 4K)
- Download audio-only (MP3, M4A, etc.)
- Support for playlists
- Beautiful real-time progress bars
- Cross-platform (Windows, macOS, Linux)
- Single binary - no dependencies to install
- Fast startup - &lt; 1ms
- No ads, no paywalls, just downloads

## Requirements

This package requires:
- ffmpeg (install with: `choco install ffmpeg`)
- yt-dlp (install with: `pip install yt-dlp`)

## Usage

```
pull-vids "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID"
pull-vids -a "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID"  # Audio only
pull-vids -q 720p "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID"  # Specific quality
```
